title: Gigi_Monologue
---
Gigi: It's high. Higher than I thought.
Gigi: Wow... I didn't think it would be this high.
Gigi: It's almost hypnotizing.
Gigi: Maybe I should have called my boss to quit first...
Gigi: Meh, whatever.
Gigi: What difference does it make in the end? One more step. One step forward, and everything stops.
Gigi: Stopping. Being on pause. Frozen in the moment. Isn't that kind of what I've been looking for?
Gigi: Does it hurt?
Gigi: I should already know. I've read, I've seen… but in reality, is it instant?
Gigi: And even if it was… why does it even matter to me?
Gigi: This is ridiculous. I'm still asking myself questions, even now.
Gigi: I always overthink.
Gigi: Is that my problem? Always thinking, never acting?
Gigi: I'm tired.
Gigi: Tired of being tired.
Gigi: Tired of pretending.
Gigi: Of playing a role whose script I've forgotten.
Gigi: …
Gigi: My life is a joke.
Gigi: 28 years old and nothing to show for it. Nothing.
Gigi: A career that only exists on paper. A shitty job where I'm invisible.
Gigi: Entire days pretending to be motivated while I wither away.
Gigi: Colleagues who don't even know who I am. And me, do I even know who I am?
Gigi: I've failed everything.
Gigi: School, friendships, love, ambition… everything others seem to succeed in effortlessly.
Gigi: 28 years old and I already feel like I've ruined it all. Like there's no way to fix anything.
Gigi: What if it's too late?
Gigi: They say the survival instinct is stronger than anything. But if you smother it long enough… it eventually goes silent, right?
Gigi: Is that what I did? Suffocate it little by little until it disappeared?
Gigi: Just one step…
Gigi: A step toward the end, or a step toward a new beginning?
Gigi: …
Gigi: Why am I hesitating?
Gigi: Because maybe… a part of me still hopes?
Gigi: … No one.
Gigi: Of course.
Gigi: I'm always alone, so why would that change now?
Gigi: But then… why am I still talking, even if no one is listening?
Gigi: Because I still exist, somewhere.
Gigi: Maybe… maybe I'm waiting for something?
Gigi: A sign? A voice? A breath?
Gigi: Is that really impossible?
Gigi: Idiot. This isn't a story, there's no miracle coming.
Gigi: But if I were waiting for a miracle…
Gigi: That would mean I still have hope, right?
Gigi: …
Gigi: And yet…
Gigi: Just one more second.
Gigi: One more second…
Gigi: … And then, we'll see.
Gigi: …
Gigi: No. Not this time.
Gigi: I'm tired of waiting, tired of hoping.
Gigi: There's no answer.
Gigi: There has never been an answer.
Gigi: So I might as well just end it.
===

title: Gigi_Monologue_2
---
Gigi: Ah... I can't believe I did it.
Gigi: I really am falling.
Gigi: What did I do wrong to end up doing something like that?
Gigi: All these girls in my office... they all looked so special...
Gigi: As if they all had fulfilling lives...
Gigi: Living like princesses.
Gigi: If only I could have feel fulfilled just one time...
Gigi: Maybe It would have stop me from jumping.
Gigi: Why am I thinking about the past anyway? Screw that.
===

title: Gigi_Monologue_3
---
Gigi: I'm... still alive?
Gigi: W-where am I? Am I in the sewers?
Gigi: ...
Gigi: It's way too high for me to reach them...
Gigi: I could let myself die here...
Gigi: ...
Gigi: ...
Gigi: Nah forget it, there is no way I'll die in... sewers urgh...
Gigi: I guess I gotta find a way out somewhere else...
===